# UI build artifacts and dependencies.
# Docker only reads the .dockerignore at the build context root, and every
# service builds with context "." (see service-map.yaml) — so per-directory
# .dockerignore files under src/ui/ are inert and these patterns have to
# live here. Leaving a stale dist/ or .angular/ in the context both bloats
# the transfer and risks shadowing what `npm ci` + `ng build` produce in the
# image.
**/node_modules
src/ui/*/dist
src/ui/*/.angular
src/ui/*/out-tsc
src/ui/*/__screenshots__

# Rust build artifacts
**/target

# Python cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.Python
**/*.egg
**/*.egg-info

# Environment files
**/.env*
!**/.env.example

# Version control
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# OS files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# IDE files
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/**.swp
**/**.swo

# Logs
**/logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Test coverage
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Documentation
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Temporary files
**/tmp
**/temp
**/.cache
